sysh (0.6.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: transient scope units now get a unique name per exec — a
    script or console session is one process, so every line named
    the same unit and systemd refused to load it ("already loaded",
    exit 1 on alternating lines).
  * Fix: help quotes the script shebang — the sentence's semicolon
    read as part of the line and literal-minded clients copied it.
  * Fix: a traced refusal that names a denylisted interpreter now
    says interpreters belong in the shebang, not in an exec.
  * watch: expired approval requests keep their teaching line for a
    three-minute grace, then the pending panel hides itself.
  * watch: host cards count only non-zero rules, color the policy
    mode and the agent-scripts mode, drop the :22 from addresses.
  * Fix: a host with no policy answer no longer breaks the grid.
  * watch: hosts fill within seconds of opening the page (poller
    settles before first poll; fetch failures are logged).
  * watch: the priv badge explains itself on hover.
  * docs: the bash-compatibility spectrum — direct exec, console,
    lines, traced, root — as a table in usage.html and PROJECT.md,
    with what each mode gives the operator and the agent.

 -- xezpeleta <xezpeleta@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 05 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200

sysh (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Agent scripts: a root-owned directory of one-command-per-line
    scripts (#!/usr/bin/sysh), every line policy-checked and
    journaled like a direct exec (PROJECT.md 6.10).
  * Traced agent scripts: agent_scripts_mode = "traced" runs any
    shebang under a ptrace tracer; every execve in the tree is
    argv-checked, refusals fail the syscall (-EPERM). amd64-only;
    kill switch /run/sysh/traced-off (6.13).
  * Interactive console for `ssh sy@host` with a TTY: banner, help,
    cd navigation; each line through the same pipeline (6.11).
  * Teaching denies: absolute-path hints, shell-operator and
    rsync teaching lines, escape-hatch explanations (6.12).
  * Channel contract documented and taught in-band: child stdout
    untouched, JSON envelope on stderr (6.4).
  * Worked example policies: examples/diagnostic (read-only),
    examples/operational (approval channel), examples/webserver.

 -- Xabier Ezpeleta <xezpeleta@github.com>  Sun, 05 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0200

sysh (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Agent keys expire: keys.map third field `expires:` RFC3339;
    expired keys refused pre-argv; sysh auth add --ttl / rotate.
  * Root mode (mode = "root"): explicit opt-out for disposable
    hosts; deny rules only, everything else root via one wildcard
    sudoers grant; journal intact.
  * sy watch: browser alerts on new approval requests (beta).
  * Relicensed MIT -> GPLv3.

 -- Xabier Ezpeleta <xezpeleta@github.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200

sysh (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Approvals: signed FIDO2-grade channel (§9).
    - sysh approver add/list/remove: registered approver keys in
      /etc/sysh/approvers; sk-* (hardware-backed) keys recommended,
      software keys allowed with a warning.
    - sysh approve --show / --sig: sign the exact request bytes with
      ssh-keygen -Y sign (namespace sysh-approve) and submit; SSHSIG
      verified in-process (golang.org/x/crypto/ssh) — no ssh-keygen
      dependency on the verify path. Signature bound to the request
      content, namespace, and a registered key; requests stay TTL'd
      and single-use.
  * sysh-mcp: `sy mcp` stdio MCP server (§10) for agent harnesses —
    tools sy_exec, sy_docs, sy_policy over plain SSH as the sy user;
    approval-required (exit 30) surfaced with the request id; no
    approval power of any kind in tool space.
  * sy client (same deb): `sy approve [host] <id>` / `sy approvals`
    — the operator-side approval ceremony. Fetches the exact request
    bytes from the server over the operator's root SSH channel,
    displays the server-recorded argv, recomputes the request id
    locally before anything reaches the signing gesture, then signs
    (sk-* keys: insert-your-YubiKey loop + PIN + touch inside
    ssh-keygen) and submits. A TTY-only confirmation prompt sits
    between the display and the signature; piped stdin is refused.

 -- xezpeleta <xezpeleta@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

sysh (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 1: argv-policy login shell for AI agents.
    - Gateway: printable-ASCII argv split, exact-length matching, opt-in
      rest patterns, deny rules with prefix semantics, per-rule timeouts
      with process-group kill backstop, 1 MiB output cap.
    - Containment: NoNewPrivs re-exec, seccomp not yet (phase 2),
      systemd scope execution with no-scope fallback, ptrace_scope=1.
    - Events: journald records with kernel attestation (_UID, _AUDIT_
      LOGINUID), key attribution (fingerprint, key id), policy hash,
      pre/post phases; auditd integration (sysh_exec, sysh_policy,
      sysh_lockdown keys).
  * Control channel: auth add/list/remove (option allowlist, canonical
    comma-separated authorized_keys lines, fingerprint dedup), policy
    install/lint (denylist, warn-ack classes, permissive gated on
    active auditd rules), doctor (22 checks), lockdown, journal-group.
  * Packaging: systemd tmpfiles, sy user with shell-takeover refusal,
    sshd drop-in with validated rollback, audit rules with uid
    substitution, selfcheck in postinst.

